Q: SELECT all rows and count rows using CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder with just one trip to the database? A: <p>Your model method only needs to return the 2d payload to the controller (it doesn't need to be tasked with also counting the rows).</p>
<pre><code>public function getAll(): array
{
    return $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('records')-&gt;result_array();
}
</code></pre>
<p>In your controller, you can just call <code>count()</code> if you need it at that level. If the count is only needed by the view, then only call <code>count()</code> in the view.</p>
<hr />
<p>If there are times when you only want the count of all rows and don't need the actual row data (in a single server request), then yes, it is sensible to dedicate a method to this singular responsibility (but I've never found myself in this situation).</p>
<pre><code>public function countAll(): int
{
    return $this-&gt;db-&gt;count_all('records');
}    
</code></pre>
